{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/479143-touchstones-and-travel","id":479143,"title":"Touchstones and Travel","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-13T08:58:45-07:00","id":479143,"title":"Touchstones and Travel","content":"I would like my players to be able to travel, but Touchstones (examples) <i>seem</i> to require that they always stay in the same place. While this makes sense thematically, I would still like them to be able to Travel. Am I misunderstanding this? Or, if not, what should I do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3927-demon15","name":"Demon15","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T09:04:06-07:00","id":479162,"title":"","content":"Keep on the phone with your Touchstone and accept the possibility that they may be vulnerable, or make sure they're safe before you go anywhere.<br /> <br /> Your daughter doesn't stop being your daughter just because you can't get late night coffee and have to keep it to skype calls, but if you're in France and she's in New York, there's not much you can do when your rival coterie busts down her door mid-call to take her away.<br /> <br /> Touchstones where you have no means of checking in with them will be much tougher if not impossible, particularly before the 21st century.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T09:04:45-07:00","id":479164,"title":"","content":"Unless the Touchstone is a location/building, it should be able to travel in some sense. <br /> <br /> Now, certain touchstones are going to be harder to get to travel than others, and depending on if you want that to be a focus of your game, you can make it dramatic or not. If you don't want it dramatic, just have players choose touchstones with a travel theme (truckers, flight attendants, nomads, traveling art shows or bands, etc).<br /> <br /> If you do want it to be dramatic, then you can explore issues like a Vampire getting their touchstone fired from the local job, so they have more time to travel. Of messing up their local romance and catfishing some distant romantic contact, things like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T09:48:16-07:00","id":479185,"title":"","content":"Depends a bit on how much and how long they are away from their Touchstones. I have run it so that occasionally being away from your Touchstones for a few weeks (with good reason) is not a problem and if a character needs their Willpower fix we run a flashback with the Touchstone in question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T10:24:34-07:00","id":479225,"title":"","content":"I set the Campaign in the Dark Ages and want them to be able to go to cool places to uncover mysteries. However, this is the (fake) Middle Ages. I guess each of them could travel with a retinue of retainers, but that seems kind of weird to me. We like touchstones, just not sure how to make this work.<br /> <br /> I wonder if I could hack a less effective version of it - like - do something very human, e.g.<br /> Player who is (actually well educated) Mideval Physican - go do some charity healing work wherever Nuns hang out;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3927-demon15","name":"Demon15","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T10:25:16-07:00","id":479226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/479143-touchstones-and-travel?p=479185#post479185\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends a bit on how much and how long they are away from their Touchstones. I have run it so that occasionally being away from your Touchstones for a few weeks (with good reason) is not a problem and if a character needs their Willpower fix we run a flashback with the Touchstone in question.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't like the flashback thing, (they still got access to Mask/Dirge and they're away from touchstone - makes sense it's harder to get WP), but other than that this looks like a fine solution <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T12:29:29-07:00","id":479345,"title":"","content":"Have them send letters by Ghoul courier or Gallows Post. If the touchstone is of a lower class and doesn't know how to read or write, the courier can read the letters out loud and take down a dictated response. Or teach them, that works too. I actually think the idea is rather touching.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-13-2015, 03:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T13:40:35-07:00","id":479434,"title":"","content":"+1'ing Charlaquin's idea. I had the children of a PC in my last Dark Ages VtM game correspond with her via post, and it worked out great. Writing letters with the player in real-time was a fun change of pace from roleplaying face-to-face interactions, it felt historically authentic, and the letters themselves were d'aww-worthy.<br /> <br /> There's a reason your grandparents save all their old love letters to each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T16:04:01-07:00","id":479583,"title":"","content":"I love this! it's so period!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T16:52:09-07:00","id":480932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/479143-touchstones-and-travel?p=479164#post479164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you do want it to be dramatic, then you can explore issues like a Vampire getting their touchstone fired from the local job, so they have more time to travel. Or messing up their local romance and catfishing some distant romantic contact, things like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Screwing up a Touchstone's life just to free them up for a Road Trip?<br /> <br /> I am hard-pressed to think of a better example of the kindred-mortal dynamic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T04:41:19-07:00","id":481261,"title":"","content":"&quot;Hey, yeah, what's up? So I wanted to go to New York for the weekend, remember I told you? Yeah, and you said it was your one year anniversary with your boyfriend so you couldn't? Yeah. Well, I killed him. Happy anniversary. Pack your bags.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T15:53:05-07:00","id":488807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/479143-touchstones-and-travel?p=480932#post480932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Screwing up a Touchstone's life just to free them up for a Road Trip?<br /> <br /> I am hard-pressed to think of a better example of the kindred-mortal dynamic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded.<br /> <br /> My current nWoD game has travel as a plot point, so working out the vampire character's Touchstones and how they might travel with her is going to be interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T15:50:46-07:00","id":491020,"title":"","content":"Given that some players (especially those who started out with V:tM and other OWoD storylines) grew up in the dawn of the internet era and made friends online (especially if the friend is overseas and/or an MMO gaming buddy), I can envision someone actually having a Touchstone that they've never met in the flesh, having only seen them in photos or video/Skype style chat, and only heard their voice in the same fashion. I actually had toyed with the idea of a character who had a long-time friend and gaming companion as one of his Touchstones in this way.<br /> <br /> Being in touch with them through similar electronic means might make that kind of contact easier, although it's also kind of a two-edged sword; if you don't have access to a means to contact them (especially for extended periods of time), you're not nearly as connected to them. Likewise, it might be harder for an enemy to harm said Touchstone directly, but as time passes and people change, that connection\u2014not the electronic linkage\u2014could also change or fade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 04-24-2015, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T16:00:38-07:00","id":491030,"title":"","content":"That would be very difficult, given that the OP was asking for a campaign set in the dark ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-24T16:54:18-07:00","id":491077,"title":"","content":"True; though I was referring based on the original more general post. (I didn't notice the dark ages note until a few posts down.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}